# See https://docs.github.com/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files for more about ignoring files.

# ── Frontend (Angular, under frontend/) ─────────────────────────────────
# Compiled output
/frontend/dist
/frontend/docs
/frontend/tmp
/frontend/out-tsc
/frontend/bazel-out

# Node
/frontend/node_modules
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# Angular cache
/frontend/.angular/cache

# The app ships no data of its own — every read goes through the backend API — so
# frontend/data/ should never come back. Ignored rather than merely deleted: the payloads
# that used to live there are the only surviving copy of the wwmdb data (archived in the
# backend repo's backfill-data/), and re-committing them here would republish a roster
# carrying UID/PID, the identity keys the Register flow trusts. This repo is public.
/frontend/data/

# The .NET backend lives in its own private repository. It was vendored here once and
# removed, so older checkouts still have the files on disk. Ignored so a `git add -A`
# cannot quietly re-publish the private source (or its bin/obj) into this public repo.
/backend/

# ── IDEs and editors ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.project
.classpath
.c9/
*.launch
.settings/
*.sublime-workspace
.vs/

